---
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Learn how The Wonder Years Day Nursery approaches safeguarding, supports children with SEND and adapts care and learning around each child’s individual needs." />
    <title>Safeguarding, SEND and Inclusion | The Wonder Years Day Nursery</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}styles/global.css`} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div class="wireframe-banner">Safeguarding, SEND and Inclusion · Content and image placement for review</div>
    <SiteHeader current="about" />
    <main id="main">
      <section class="section hero">
        <div class="container hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">Safe, individual and inclusive care</p>
            <h1>Safeguarding, SEND and Inclusion</h1>
            <p class="lead">Every child should feel safe, known and able to take part in nursery life.</p>
            <p>Safeguarding is central to the way the nursery operates. The team also works to understand each child as an individual, adapting care, learning and support around their needs.</p>
            <p>If there is anything you would like the nursery to know about your child before they start, please speak to the team.</p>
            <div class="button-row">
              <a class="button" href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact the nursery</a>
              <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}meet-the-team/`}>Meet the team</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="image-placeholder hero-image" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a calm, welcoming nursery environment"><span>Welcoming nursery image placeholder</span><small>A calm nursery environment or staff member preparing an activity</small></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-muted">
        <div class="container split-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Safeguarding comes first</p>
            <h2>A responsibility shared by everyone</h2>
            <p>All staff receive safeguarding training. Updates and quizzes during staff meetings help ensure that knowledge is reviewed and retained.</p>
            <h3>The nursery’s safeguarding leads are:</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><a href={`${base}meet-the-team/`}><strong>Mandy Barker</strong></a>, Designated Safeguarding Lead;</li>
              <li><a href={`${base}meet-the-team/`}><strong>Rachael Jones</strong></a>, Safeguarding Lead; and</li>
              <li><a href={`${base}meet-the-team/`}><strong>Kirsty Burke</strong></a>, Safeguarding Lead.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>They support staff, respond to concerns and help make sure the nursery follows its safeguarding responsibilities.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="funded-hours-card">
            <p class="eyebrow">Raising a concern</p>
            <h3>Speak to the nursery</h3>
            <p>Parents and carers should speak to the Nursery Manager or a safeguarding lead if they have a concern about:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>their own child;</li>
              <li>something their child has said;</li>
              <li>a change in their child’s behaviour;</li>
              <li>something they have seen or heard; or</li>
              <li>any aspect of safety or wellbeing within the nursery.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The nursery will respond in line with its safeguarding responsibilities and procedures.</p>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact the nursery</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-accent">
        <div class="container split-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Supporting children with SEND</p>
            <h2>Understanding strengths and support needs</h2>
            <p>SEND means special educational needs and disabilities. Some needs are identified before a child starts nursery, while others may become clearer as the child settles and develops.</p>
            <p>The nursery works with parents and carers to understand:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>the child’s strengths and interests;</li>
              <li>how they communicate, learn and take part;</li>
              <li>where they may need additional help; and</li>
              <li>what support may help them progress.</li>
            </ul>
            <p><a href={`${base}meet-the-team/`}><strong>Kirsty Burke</strong></a> is the nursery’s SENDCO and helps coordinate support for children with additional needs.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Every child is an individual</p>
            <h2>Adapting care and learning</h2>
            <p>The nursery considers each child’s needs and learning style when planning care, activities and support.</p>
            <ul class="adaptation-list">
              <li>how an activity is introduced;</li>
              <li>the resources used;</li>
              <li>the level of adult support;</li>
              <li>the nursery environment;</li>
              <li>routines and transitions; and</li>
              <li>how information is communicated.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The aim is to give every child meaningful opportunities to participate, develop and progress.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container split-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Working with parents and carers</p>
            <h2>Families know their children best</h2>
            <p>Open communication helps the nursery understand what is important for each child and whether any additional support may be needed.</p>
            <p>Families are encouraged to share relevant information about development, communication, routines, health or sensory needs, existing professional support and approaches that work well at home.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Support that develops</p>
            <h2>Responding as children grow</h2>
            <p>Children’s needs can change as they grow, settle into a new room or prepare for school.</p>
            <p>The team observes children as they play, communicate and take part in everyday experiences. Where additional support is needed, the nursery can adapt its approach and discuss this with the child’s family.</p>
            <p>The purpose is to understand what each child needs to feel included and able to progress at their own pace.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-muted">
        <div class="container split-grid reverse">
          <div class="image-placeholder landscape" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for inclusive activity resources"><span>Inclusive activity image placeholder</span><small>An inclusive activity area, sensory resources or adaptable nursery equipment</small></div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Inclusion across the nursery</p>
            <h2>Belonging in everyday nursery life</h2>
            <p>Activities and routines can be adapted so children with different needs and ways of learning can participate alongside their peers.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>take part in activities and build relationships;</li>
              <li>communicate in ways that work for them;</li>
              <li>develop confidence and independence;</li>
              <li>feel that they belong within their room; and</li>
              <li>move between rooms and on to school with appropriate support.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container funding-panel">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Before your child starts</p>
            <h2>Share information early</h2>
            <p>If your child has an identified need, receives professional support or may need adjustments at nursery, please discuss this with the team before their start date.</p>
            <p>Sharing information early gives the nursery an opportunity to understand what may be needed. If you are unsure whether something is relevant, you are still welcome to raise it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="button-stack">
            <a class="button" href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact the nursery</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="tel:01215566979">Call 0121 556 6979</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="final-cta">
        <div class="container">
          <h2>Speak to the team</h2>
          <p>Discuss safeguarding, SEND, inclusion or your child’s individual needs with the nursery.</p>
          <div class="button-row centred">
            <a class="button button-light" href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact the nursery</a>
            <a class="button button-outline-light" href="tel:01215566979">Call 0121 556 6979</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>
